             gearmesh-medium-train-089 gearmesh-medium-train-090 gearmesh-medium-train-091 gearmesh-medium-train-092
             gearmesh-medium-train-093 gearmesh-medium-train-094 gearmesh-medium-train-095 gearmesh-medium-train-096
             gearmesh-medium-train-097 gearmesh-medium-train-098 gearmesh-medium-train-099 gearmesh-medium-train-100)

  (:provenance
    (:source "Authored for this corpus, after nvidia-isaac/Isaac-cap's
              `gear_insertion` -- three Factory gears placed on a plate and
              scored SEATED AND STILL, at post offsets stated as constants. Two
              things change. The peg spacing is DERIVED from the gears' pitch
              radii, module * [z_a + z_b] / 2, so a board that does not mesh
              cannot be authored, and the score is the assembly WORKING -- a
              motor pinion drives the first station, and success is every gear
              turning at its own ratio once the button latches, so a gear
              missing from the middle stops everything downstream of it. Gears
              are generated involute profiles decomposed into one convex prism
              per tooth, because MuJoCo collides a mesh as its hull and a gear
              imported whole is a disc. Physics regime probed before authoring:
              see tasks/gear_mesh/rigs/gear_bench.py and tests/test_gear_mesh.py.")
  )
)
